  "endPos": 4109,
  "detail":
  "```lean\nEquiv.left_inv.{u_1, u_2} {α : Sort u_1} {β : Sort u_2} (self : α ≃ β) : Function.LeftInverse self.invFun self.toFun\n```\n***\n*import Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Defs*",
  "definitionStartPos": {"line": 66, "column": 12},
  "definitionPath":
  "/Users/hattoriseiji/Autoinformalization/ExportInfos/./.lake/packages/mathlib//Mathlib/Logic/Equiv/Defs.lean",
  "definitionEndPos": {"line": 66, "column": 20}},
 {"startPos": 4113,
  "moduleName": "Init.Prelude",
  "kind": "theorem",
  "fullName": "Eq.symm",
  "endPos": 4117,
  "detail":
  "```lean\nEq.symm.{u} {α : Sort u} {a b : α} (h : a = b) : b = a\n```\n***\nEquality is symmetric: if `a = b` then `b = a`.\n\nBecause this is in the `Eq` namespace, if you have a variable `h : a = b`,\n`h.symm` can be used as shorthand for `Eq.symm h` as a proof of `b = a`.\n\nFor more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality)\n\n***\n*import Init.Prelude*",
  "definitionStartPos": {"line": 323, "column": 8},
  "definitionPath":
  "/Users/hattoriseiji/.elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.10.0-rc2/src/lean/Init/Prelude.lean",
  "definitionEndPos": {"line": 323, "column": 15}},
